bionic/Android: fix struct termios breakage in stress-pty.c

stress-ng V0.22.02 includes <asm/termbits.h> with `termios` renamed to
`ioctl_termios` so it can use the kernel UAPI struct alongside the libc
one.  On bionic, <termios.h> is itself implemented on top of the Linux
UAPI headers and struct termios is defined inside <asm-generic/termbits.h>
under the __ASM_GENERIC_TERMBITS_H include guard.  Processing that header
first with the rename macro sets the guard, so the later <termios.h> is
skipped and struct termios is never defined:

  bits/termios_inlines.h:50:47: error: incomplete definition of type
      'const struct termios'
  stress-pty.c:204:20: error: variable has incomplete type 'struct termios'

There is no need for the rename trick on bionic: bionic's struct termios
is the kernel UAPI struct, so include <termios.h> and alias ioctl_termios
to termios instead.  Other platforms keep the upstream behaviour.

This patch targets stress-ng V0.22.02.  scripts/common.sh skips patches
that no longer apply, so once upstream fixes this it becomes a no-op.

--- a/stress-pty.c
+++ b/stress-pty.c
@@ -20,6 +20,16 @@

 #if defined(HAVE_ASM_TERMBITS_H) &&		\
     defined(HAVE_ASM_TERMBITS_STRUCT_TERMIOS)
+#if defined(__ANDROID__)
+/*
+ *  bionic's <termios.h> is implemented on top of the Linux UAPI struct
+ *  termios.  Including <asm/termbits.h> with termios renamed would set
+ *  __ASM_GENERIC_TERMBITS_H, so the later <termios.h> could never define
+ *  struct termios.  Alias ioctl_termios to termios instead.
+ */
+#include <termios.h>
+#define ioctl_termios termios
+#else
 /*
  *  rename termbits termios to ioctl_termios
  */
@@ -27,6 +37,7 @@
 #include <asm/termbits.h>
 #undef termios
 #endif
+#endif

 #include <sys/ioctl.h>

